cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference the Revocation Exposure concept, please cite it as below."
title: "Revocation Exposure — Measuring the Window Between Withdrawn and Enforced Authority"
abstract: >-
  Revocation Exposure is a concept coined by Michał Piszczek describing the measurable window
  between a revocation decision and system-wide enforcement, during which a credential remains
  cryptographically valid but operationally unauthorized. It separates token theft from stale
  authority as two distinct security axes and frames revocation as a propagation race across
  every enforcement point in a distributed system, to be measured as a service level objective.
type: dataset
date-released: "2026-08-01"
